# Rust build artifacts
/target
/target-*/
# The MIR fixtures are NESTED workspaces (their own `[workspace]`), so the
# root-anchored `/target` above does not cover them. Building one -- which the
# documented `Cargo.lock` refresh procedure requires -- otherwise leaves
# untracked output a sibling lane could sweep into a commit.
crates/axeyum-verify/tests/fixtures/*/target/

# Local reference clones (recreate with scripts/fetch-references.sh)
/references/*/

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Benchmark scratch output
/bench-results/local/

# cargo-mutants working/output directory
/mutants.out/

# Public corpus tier (fetched, not committed)
/corpus/public/

# Local staging copy of the ACCESS-CONTROLLED Glaurung QF_BV representative
# capture. The `glaurung-qfbv-regular` gate auto-discovers the pinned NAS
# source (/nas4/.../glaurung-captures/) and otherwise SKIPs; point it at a
# local copy with AXEYUM_GLAURUNG_QFBV_REPRESENTATIVE_DIR. Never commit the
# capture itself — it is not public corpus data.
/corpus/glaurung-qfbv/

# Local CI transcript logs (regenerable; the committed evidence is the
# artifact JSON under bench-results/, not the log)
/artifacts/local-ci/

# mdBook generated site + mermaid runtime assets
# (regenerate with the pinned commands in `docs/internals/documentation.md`)
/book/
/mermaid.min.js
/mermaid-init.js

# WASM playground bundle (regenerate from the repository root; the out-dir is
# relative to the crate: `wasm-pack build crates/axeyum-wasm --target web --out-dir ../../docs/playground/pkg`)
/docs/playground/pkg/
.claude/
bench-results/parity-details/

# Python layer (docs/python-2026-08/01-pyo3-maturin.md): the compiled extension
# `maturin develop` drops into the source package, the wheel output directory,
# and the uv-managed virtualenv. All three are regenerable with
# `uv sync --dev && uv run maturin develop`.
python/axeyum/*.so
python/axeyum/*.pyd
/dist/
/.venv/

# L3 phase D1 (ADR-0965): the real kernel full-name inventory snapshot is
# regenerated by scripts/check-declaration-spec.py on every run from
# `examples/declaration_spec_pilot --dump-names`; it is a build artifact of
# the CURRENT tree, not a stable pin, and it changes on every declaration
# any prelude lands.
/artifacts/declaration-spec/generated/kernel-names-snapshot.txt

# Session sentinel for the /goal stop-hook. Deliberately untracked -- it is
# per-session state, not repository content. Ignored because broad `git add`
# operations kept staging it (and once swept it into a merge commit).
are_we_done

# Lane scratch from the Lean store harness; per-run, never content.
.axeyum-lean-store-cell-*/
